# Chapter One\: The Quay

The ferry leaves at seven\. Café tables fill early\, and the señor at the counter pours coffee without asking\.

## Morning Tides

Gulls argue over crusts\; the crane operators wave\, and everyone says “good morning” in three languages\. Prices – in euros – are posted by the quay\. Unicode check\: €5 and česky\.

